Despite their priority status under EU conservation policies, Spanish temporary ponds remain highly threatened and poorly documented, with existing information scattered across heterogeneous sources. TemPondS (Temporary Ponds of Peninsular Spain) fills th
is gap as a comprehensive, open-access spatial compilation integrating primary and historical records into a single, harmonised dataset. By synthesising peer-reviewed and grey literature, administrative inventories, citizen science, and expert-contributed
 d
atasets, TemPondS provides a robust baseline for research and management. Using a rigorous manual and supervised workflow, we developed a point-based dataset comprising 10,373 entries from 280 sources. Each record includes a unique ID, consensus names, co
ordinates, and legal protection status (Natura 2000 and other Protected Areas). }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\insrsid858904\charrsid5135234 
This resource ensures full source traceability through standardised metadata and is designed as a dynamic, continuously updated repository supporting future monitoring and conservation of these vulnerable ecosystems, while offering a replicable model for 
developing similar inventories elsewhere, where such catalogues are largely lacking.
